// THE VECTOR FONT — text as line art.
//
// Every classic vector game draws its score, lives, attract mode and GAME OVER
// with the same beam that draws the ships. Raster text on a line-art screen
// reads as a different game, so the layer needs a stroked face of its own.
//
// A glyph is a set of POLYLINES in a 0..1 em box, y DOWN (the engine's world
// orientation), so `y: 0` is the cap line and `y: 1` the baseline. Strokes are
// straight segments only — that is what the hardware could draw, and it is why
// the faces of the era look the way they do.
//
// Zero imports: pure data + pure maths, so both backends and the kit can share
// it with no chance of a cycle.

